 "differences": [
  "Not reproduced, so not used as checks: mean % of trials excluded (shared files give 1.28% in Experiment 1, paper 1.2%; 0.99% in Experiment 2, paper 1.9%); mean vowel duration (447.7 ms single task and 437.5 ms dual task, paper 449 and 439); mean dot coherence (60.3%, paper 59%).",
  "Experiment 2 adaptation (last 10 hold trials minus last 10 baseline trials, first 50 ms of F1 in mels, opposite sign to the shift as in the authors' analysis) gave 40.0 mel single task and 46.5 mel dual task (paper 36.6 and 44.0); washout 28.3 and 32.2 (paper 25.2 and 31.5); retention 4.3 and 20.5 (paper 0.2 and 14.8). The authors' values rest on filtered, baseline-referenced formant matrices that were not rebuilt here, so the per-trial values differ slightly from theirs.",
  "Compensation in Experiment 1 was not recomputed for the same reason."
 ],
